Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The help says that the first argument 'arglist' a "list of argument lists for secr.fit or a character vector naming such lists...". The 'dontrun' example shows the second of these forms:
par.secr.fit (c('fit0','fitb'), ncores = 2). The alternative is: par.secr.fit (list(fit0,fitb), ncores = 2) [or par.secr.fit (list(fit0=fit0,fitb=fitb), ncores = 2) if you want to name the models].
Murray

On Tue, Dec 1, 2015 at 4:36 AM, Michał Bogdziewicz <michalbo...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Hi SECR users,
